  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "How the pipelines meet",
      "items": [
        "They never call each other. load_to_neo4j writes n.embedding and vec_<label>_embedding; vector_search only opens those indexes with Neo4jVector.from_existing_index",
        "Both sides use the same six labels and the same text_props / AZURE_EMBEDDING_DEPLOYMENT, so the question vector sits in the same cosine space as the stored nodes",
        "graph_qa and graph_qa_with_context query that same Neo4j graph with Cypher (structure and context_refs), not by calling Pipeline_embeddings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "graph.py routes",
      "items": [
        "ingest is the only entry; route_question is a conditional edge, not an add_node",
        "vector search: rewrite_vector → decompose_and_route → vector_search → prompt_template_with_context → graph_qa_with_context → generate",
        "graph query: rewrite_graph → prompt_template → graph_qa → generate; chat skips retrieval and goes ingest → generate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What the thin nodes do",
      "items": [
        "prompt_template and prompt_template_with_context only forward state; the few-shot Cypher prompt is built inside get_graph_qa_chain[_with_context]",
        "rewrite_vector and rewrite_graph are the same rewrite() function under two graph.py names"
      ]
    }
  ]
